                "quoted_status_profile_username": null,
                "reply_count": 17,
                "retweet_count": 17,
                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "I\u2019ve been working for years on legislation to increase Alaska\u2019s federal match funding for Medicaid, because of our unique and challenging health care costs. I finally got it into the budget reconciliation bill with the support of all Senate Republicans and the White House. This bill would\u2019ve provided hundreds of millions of additional federal Medicaid dollars to Alaska. As far-left groups are running ads falsely claiming I support Medicaid cuts, Chuck Schumer and Senate Democrat leaders just celebrated stripping my provision for increasing Medicaid dollars for Alaska from the bill. What hypocrites.\n\nThe national party openly cutting hundreds of millions of dollars of Medicaid funding for Alaska is the Democrats. That happened today. But the fight isn\u2019t over.",
                "text_lang": "en",
