                "retweet_count": 7,
                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "Senate Democrats also successfully stripped my provision from the budget reconciliation bill addressing major cost disparities for Alaska\u2019s many rural hospitals\u2014more Senate Democrat hypocrisy on health care in Alaska. But we will keep fighting for Alaska\u2019s rural hospitals!\n\nUnfortunately, this is part of the Senate Democrats\u2019 continuing assault on so many of the positive provisions for Alaska in the budget reconciliation bill. The following provisions\u2014that we are fighting to keep in the final bill\u2014have all been fought by Chuck Schumer and Senate Democrats to strip out of the bill:\n\n\u27a1\ufe0f ANWR leases\n\u27a1\ufe0f NPR-A leases\n\u27a1\ufe0f Cook Inlet leases\n\u27a1\ufe0f Coast Guard funding for Alaska, including facilities for the new icebreaker home-ported in Juneau\n\u27a1\ufe0f Potential Arctic military bases\n\u27a1\ufe0f Border security",
